<p>Decimal 36868. Read only. Also known as <strong>VICCR4</strong>.</p>
<p>This register, together with bit 7 of $9003 (SCREEN_TEXT_HEIGHT), forms the TV
raster counter. $9004 holds bits 8-1 of the line number, so each step of 1 is two
raster lines, and bit 7 of $9003 supplies the missing low bit.</p>
<p>On a 625 line TV (PAL) this register counts between 0 and 155 and the whole
counter between 0 and 311; on NTSC the whole counter runs to 260.</p>
<p>Reading it is the usual way to time an effect to the display, though
WaitForRaster does the polling for you:</p>
<code>
// hold until the raster reaches line 0, once per frame
WaitForRaster( 0 );
SCREEN_BG_COLOR := SCREEN_BG_BLACK + WHITE;
</code>
